<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schengen Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1985</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schengen Agreement is a treaty signed on 14 June 1985 at Schengen in Luxembourg by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, Luxembourg and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to abolish checks at their common borders gradually. A convention of 1990 implemented it, and checks were lifted from 1995. Incorporated into EU law by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> in 1999, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schengen-area">Schengen Area</a> now covers most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, including some states outside the Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schengen-agreement.jpg" alt="Schengen Agreement" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zinneke · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schengen_Agreement_(1985)_signatures.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
